ests in internal/install/commit_test.go cover every AC clause. Gates: go build 0, go vet 0, gofmt clean, go test ./... 0, go test -race (install/transaction/managerlock) 0. golangci-lint exits 1 with 45 issues - expected red: the pre-change composed base produces the same 45 with identical per-linter counts, so this task adds zero new lint issues. REVIEWER ATTENTION: internal/transaction refuses symlink targets while adapters default to symlink-first mode, so per contract 6.1 step 12 the adapter/mirror LEDGERS are journaled rather than each symlink entry; symlink entries are created pre-commit and pruned only post-success so a rollback never deletes a live mirror. internal/transaction was deliberately not modified.\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-e054e1, pid=78985, exit=0)\nINDEPENDENT REVIEW DIRECTIVE 2026-07-28: review the producer outcome and existing uncommitted stacked worktree read-only; do not modify, stage, commit, or inherit the producer conclusion. Trace every AC clause through project/global/hybrid code and tests: no shared mutation before canonical home lock and complete revalidation; stale closure/activation/cache/owner/preimage/key restart behavior; deterministic cache and target classes with consumer ledger last; first-install and upgrade rollback at every failure boundary; pre-existing immutable cache preservation; cross-project concurrency without rollback clobbering another commit; journal recovery before mutation; post-commit GC warning semantics; dry-run and prior audit/build gates unchanged. Challenge the documented adapter/mirror-ledger treatment where transaction rejects symlink targets. Independently inspect the final gate archive and rerun suitable build/vet/full/scoped/race/lint-delta checks, serially. Strict six-guarantee hardened containment remains non-gating STORY-260728-327soo and must not be claimed. Attach a task-scoped ACCEPTED or CHANGES REQUESTED verdict and route status accordingly.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-27ac8a, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-27ac8a)\nReviewer cycle 1 changes requested: production-default auto/symlink adapter mirrors mutate outside the durable journal; link failure can leave a prepared journal that recovery later commits, rollback cannot restore replaced mirrors, and stale adapter pruning happens after the consumer ledger. The rollback sweep forces copy mode and omits forwarding-shim, mirror-ledger, removal, hybrid, and symlink classes. See TASK-260720-2284br_review-verdict-cycle-1.md.\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260728-27ac8a, pid=55935, exit=0)\nREWORK DIRECTIVE cycle 1 2026-07-28: continue in /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/curator/.temp/TASK-260720-1zntv0/worktree without staging or committing and preserve the stacked accepted base. Treat TASK-260720-2284br_review-verdict-cycle-1.md as mandatory input. Fix both acceptance blockers: bring default auto/symlink adapter replacement plus stale managed removals under durable transaction ownership with exact preimage restoration, deterministic pre-consumer ordering, and durable rollback for every post-prepare failure; then expand fault-injection evidence across project/global/hybrid, forwarding-shim, mirror-ledger, removal, default auto and explicit symlink paths, link-boundary recovery, and consumer-last stale pruning. Keep STORY-260728-327soo non-gating and make no hardened-isolation claims. Rerun focused/full/race/build/vet/format/task-scoped lint and attach revised implementation and gate evidence before developer handoff.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-b80d71, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-b80d71)\nRework cycle 1 started 2026-07-28. R1 root cause accepted: internal/transaction refused symlink targets, so the default auto/symlink adapter path had to mutate outside the journal. Fix per rework directive (durable transaction ownership): extend internal/transaction with an explicit second target kind (KindEntry) owning a managed directory entry as itself - digested, backed up, restored and removed as the link it is, with leaf-preserving namespace resolution. KindBytes keeps its exact current contract so accepted link-refusal guarantees and tests stay intact. Adapter mirror entries and stale adapter removals become ordinary journaled targets in classes 60 and 80, both before the consumer ledger at 90; Mirror.Link and Mirror.PruneStale are removed so nothing mutates between Prepare and Commit.\nREWORK CYCLE 1 COMPLETE, ready for review. R1 root cause accepted and reversed at its source: internal/transaction refused symbolic links in every role, so the production-default auto adapter mode had no journaled way to publish a mirror entry. Added an explicit second target kind - KindBytes keeps its exact contract, links refused, path fully resolved; KindEntry owns a managed directory entry that may be a link, digested by its destination string, leaf-preserving namespace resolution, Lstat identity. Additive: kind and link_target are omitempty, existing digests unchanged, links inside trees still refused, every accepted transaction test passes untouched including the two asserting DigestPath and copyTarget reject links. Adapters now emit targets only: Mirror.Link and Mirror.PruneStale deleted, mirror entries are class 60 targets, stale entries are class 80 removals, both before the consumer ledger at 90, and an already-correct link produces no target. runCommit runs Prepare immediately followed by Commit, so no ordinary post-prepare failure can leave a prepared journal. Removed the superseded direct-mutation adapter API. R2: fixtures now use the production-default auto mode; the sweep injects a failure in every class of two scenarios - project+hybrid over context, runtime, canonical shim, env, adapter ledger, removal, consumer, and global over context, forwarding shim, adapter ledger, mirror ledger, removal - with coverage enforced, since a class that is not produced cannot be failed and its install would succeed. New focused tests cover auto and explicit symlink mirror rollback with Lstat/Readlink evidence plus a recovery pass proving no journal survives, stale-removal-before-consumer in all three modes, and stale-removal rollback; 7 new transaction tests; adapters tests rewritten to the staged API; internal/staging gained its own tests. Per orchestrator directive the acceptance suite moved to internal/install/atomicity so ordinary go test ./... stays green under the standard 10m package timeout with no override and no class dropped: internal/install 212.7s, atomicity 360.1s. GATES: gofmt 0 files, go build 0, go vet 0, go test ./... -count=1 exit 0 at CI defaults, go test -race -timeout 45m over install/atomicity/transaction/managerlock/staging/adapters exit 0 with zero data races, task-scope golangci-lint including transaction exit 0 with 0 issues. Repo-wide golangci-lint exits 1 with 45 issues, byte-identical per-linter counts to the pre-change base (diffed), so zero new; Lint clean is left UNCHECKED honestly. REVIEWER ATTENTION: internal/transaction is modified this cycle - Event gained LivePath for ordering proofs, existingNamespaceAncestor now skips symlinks because pathconf on a dangling link answers ENOENT, and validateIndependentTargetNamespaces remains O(n^2) per saveJournal which is pre-existing and now visible with ~20 targets. No hardened-isolation claim; STORY-260728-327soo stays non-gating. Darwin/arm64 only.\nORCHESTRATOR HANDOFF 2026-07-28: producer runtime was cancelled only after it persisted the rework outcome and complete gate archive, then stopped making progress. Checklist item Lint clean is accepted at task scope: every package modified by this task passes golangci-lint with zero issues; the repo-wide 45 findings are proven inherited with zero delta and remain outside this task scope.\nINDEPENDENT REVIEW DIRECTIVE cycle 2 2026-07-28: inspect /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/curator/.temp/TASK-260720-1zntv0/worktree read-only; do not edit, stage, commit, publish, or inherit the producer verdict. Treat TASK-260720-2284br_review-verdict-cycle-1.md as the acceptance baseline and verify R1/R2 are actually closed: KindEntry must journal default auto and explicit symlink mirrors with exact Lstat/Readlink preimage restore; KindBytes must preserve its prior link-refusal contract; stale removals/classes 60 and 80 must commit before consumer class 90; no post-Prepare path may later recover as an unintended commit; project/global/hybrid fault injection must produce and fail context, runtime, canonical/forwarding shim, env, adapter/mirror ledger, removal, and consumer classes without shared-state false coverage. Inspect the rework outcome and gate archive, rerun targeted independent checks proportionate to risk, and account honestly for task-scoped lint vs inherited repo-wide findings. The strict six-guarantee containment story STORY-260728-327soo remains separate/non-gating and must not be claimed. Attach a cycle-2 ACCEPTED or CHANGES REQUESTED verdict and route status accordingly.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-2469cd, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-2469cd)\nReviewer cycle 2 changes requested: cycle-1 symlink journaling and class-sweep findings are closed, but hybrid/Skillfile.json is read into the effective closure before the home lock and is absent from optimistic observations. A read-only overlay regression removes skill-h in OnStaged; the install returns ok, reports no restart, and commits the stale hybrid context. Required: observe/recheck activation inputs under the home lock, restartClosure on mismatch, and add regression coverage. See TASK-260720-2284br_review-verdict-cycle-2.md.\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260728-2469cd, pid=29568, exit=0)\nREWORK DIRECTIVE cycle 2 2026-07-28: continue only in /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/curator/.temp/TASK-260720-1zntv0/worktree; preserve the stacked uncommitted state and do not stage, commit, publish, or alter unrelated accepted work. Treat TASK-260720-2284br_review-verdict-cycle-2.md and the reviewer scratch overlay/log under .temp/TASK-260720-2284br/review as mandatory evidence. Close R3 exactly: add every activation/closure input read before the canonical home lock to the optimistic observation set, at minimum scopes.HybridManifestPath(cfg.Home()); recheck under the lock before cache publication or target staging; any mismatch must return restartClosure and rebuild the effective closure. Audit the other closure inputs and either observe them or prove their lock/frozen-snapshot stability. Add a permanent pre-home-lock mutation regression covering removed and retargeted hybrid declarations and proving no stale context or adapter mirror commits. Preserve accepted R1/R2 behavior and tests. Start with the reviewer regression/focused packages; after green, run format/build/vet, ordinary full suite, proportionate race, and pinned lint, attach cycle-2 implementation/gate evidence, then developer handoff. Hardened containment remains separate/non-gating STORY-260728-327soo.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-eb5a56, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-eb5a56)\nRework cycle 2 in progress 2026-07-28. R3 root cause confirmed at its source: curator hybrid add|rm call scopes.AddHybridDecl/RemoveHybridDecl straight from cmd/curator/main.go:985,994 under no project, key, or home lock, so the machine-home hybrid activation manifest projectAttempt reads at step 5 could move at any point before the commit. Fix: the observation set and its path map now start at step 5 instead of step 16, and scopes.HybridManifestPath(cfg.Home()) is observed under key activation/hybrid-manifest. Ordering is digest-then-read on purpose - a writer racing the read leaves a recorded digest that no longer matches the file so the recheck restarts, whereas read-then-digest would record the writer bytes while the closure came from the bytes we read and commit stale activation. recheck already maps a generation difference to restartClosure and runCommit already calls it after recovery and before both cache publication and target staging, so no control flow changed. Closure-input audit completed and recorded in the observations doc comment; the user configuration is documented as a boundary, not claimed safe. 4 new tests in internal/install/atomicity/activation_test.go: a stable-manifest control that must NOT restart, plus removed, retargeted, and newly-applicable declarations. Negative control run: with the single observe lin