    17	// A declaration document is one shared file whose *bytes* select installed
    18	// content: the project manifest, the machine-wide manifest, the project
    19	// development substitution manifest, and the machine-home hybrid activation
    20	// manifest. Every one of them is read in the window before the manager-home lock
    21	// by a writer that takes none of this run's locks (Spec §6.1 step 6), so each is
    22	// an optimistic observation revalidated under the lock in step 10.
    23	//
    24	// An observation is only sound if its recorded generation belongs to the bytes
    25	// the closure was actually resolved from. Digesting the path and then reading it
    26	// as a second, separate operation does not give that: a supported
    27	// A -> B -> A rewrite around the read leaves both the recorded and the rechecked
    28	// digest at A while the closure was built from the transient B, and the run
    29	// commits context, shims, adapters, and consumer state for a declaration set
    30	// that is neither the one it recorded nor the one on disk. `curator add|remove`,
    31	// `curator global add|remove`, and `curator hybrid add|rm` all rewrite their
    32	// manifest in place with os.WriteFile, so that window is not hypothetical.
    33	//
    34	// readDocument therefore reads a declaration document exactly *once* and returns
    35	// the bytes together with the generation of those exact bytes. The parser
    36	// consumes the returned payload, so "the generation we recorded" and "the bytes
    37	// we parsed" are the same object by construction and cannot drift apart. A torn
    38	// read is safe for the same reason: whatever bytes came back are what the parse
    39	// saw and what the generation covers, so the under-lock recheck sees the settled
    40	// file, reports a change, and restarts instead of committing.
    41	
    42	// declarationGenerationDomain separates declaration generations from every other
    43	// digest in the manager. A generation is only ever compared with another
    44	// generation of the same document, so it needs no cross-format meaning.
    45	var declarationGenerationDomain = []byte("curator-declaration-generation-v1\x00")
    46	
    47	// documentAbsent is the generation of a document that is not there. It is
    48	// explicit so the recheck can tell "still absent" from "appeared", exactly like
    49	// transaction.DigestAbsent does for a target preimage.
    50	const documentAbsent = "absent"
    51	
    52	// afterDocumentOpen is nil in production. Tests assign it to write a declaration
    53	// document in the window between the open and the read, which is the only window
    54	// an in-place writer can use to make a parse consume bytes a separate path
    55	// digest would have missed, and prove that the recorded generation still belongs
    56	// to the bytes the parse actually consumed.
    57	var afterDocumentOpen func(path string)
    58	
    59	// document is one immutable read of a declaration document.
    60	type document struct {
    61		// payload is the exact bytes read, and the only bytes any parser may see.
    62		payload []byte
    63		// exists reports whether the document was present at all. An absent document
    64		// has no payload and each caller applies its own absent semantics.
    65		exists bool
    66		// generation identifies payload, or documentAbsent when exists is false.
    67		generation string
    68	}
